# GitHub Packages — REQUIRED to download @rogeriobatista/*
# Copy to ~/.npmrc (user) or project .npmrc. Do NOT commit real tokens.
#
# Both lines below are mandatory for install/npx from Packages:
#   1) @rogeriobatista:registry=…  — resolve the scope on GitHub Packages
#      (without it, npm looks on registry.npmjs.org → typically 404)
#   2) //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=… — auth for private packages
#      (PAT / GITHUB_TOKEN with at least `read:packages`; without it → 401)
#
# Export GITHUB_TOKEN (or NODE_AUTH_TOKEN) in the environment; keep ${…} in the file.
# For publish CI, use write:packages + NODE_AUTH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN secrets.
#
# Alternative without Packages: clone the repo and use `npm run setup` + local npx.

@rogeriobatista:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}

# Optional: if your GitHub username differs from the package scope owner,
# also set:
# //npm.pkg.github.com/:username=YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME
